    text: "The Two Seeds. Two small seeds lay side by side in the dark earth during the early spring. The first seed was very brave. 'I want to grow!' she said. 'I want to push my roots deep and see the beautiful world above the soil. I want to feel the warm sun on my face and bloom.' The second seed was very shy and cautious. 'I am afraid,' he replied. 'If I push my head into the air, a big bird might eat me. If I grow a flower, someone might pull me out of the ground. It is much safer to stay here in the dark where it is quiet.' The first seed pushed through the dirt. Soon, she became a tall, strong plant with many green leaves. Meanwhile, the second seed stayed hidden under the soil, waiting for a safe time that came at no point. One afternoon, a hungry chicken walked through the garden. The sun was hot, so the chicken stopped to rest in the shadow of the tall plant. While sitting there, the chicken scratched the dirt. It found the cautious seed and ate it for lunch.",
